3826 - Senior Associate, Sports &amp; Entertainment - Development, UK

Role Summary and Impact

As Senior Associate, you will work as a key member of the WPP Media Sports &amp; Entertainment team delivering industry-leading content solutions across a range of WPP Media clients.&nbsp;&nbsp;

The role will involve planning and activating multidisciplinary creative solutions &amp; partnerships across TV, digital, social, audio and print with the inclusion of talent and experiential activations.

Working alongside the wider team, you will build strong relationships with your clients and act as a specialist advisor to them to maximise their content partnership opportunities. &nbsp;You will also work closely with a variety of media and production partners, collaborating with them to create best-in-class partnerships that will help meet our client’s business needs.&nbsp;

In this role, you will:

As a Senior Associate within the WPP Media Sports &amp; Entertainment team, you will be a key member of the team supporting the wider department to deliver outstanding content solutions to clients.&nbsp;&nbsp;

You will be responsible for working with the Managers, Directors and Leads in the team on answering client briefs and delivering campaigns across TV, digital, social, audio and print with the inclusion of talent and experiential activations.

Other core responsibilities include:

• Planning and Delivery: Working on projects including generating creative executions/ideas, reviewing partner responses, activation, delivery &amp; project management, and reporting.&nbsp;&nbsp;

• Campaign Management: Bringing the campaign/partnership to life by supporting with project management which includes managing status calls, timelines, content approvals &amp; media delivery.&nbsp;&nbsp;

• Client Servicing: Working with clients to handle requests in a professional, timely, and accurate manner whilst building strong and effective relationships.&nbsp;

• Media: Good knowledge of media including the media landscape &amp; channels and media activation process including media plans and reporting.&nbsp;&nbsp;

• Commercials: A basic understanding of the WPP Media commercial model and internal processes including media bookings and finance.&nbsp;&nbsp;

• Team: A strong team player, supportive and collaborative with colleagues, keen to learn and develop from others as well as sharing their own expertise amongst their team.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;

• Innovation &amp; Collaboration: Building strong relationships with media partners and actively seeking out interesting trends/ industry updates to keep team and clients up to date.&nbsp;&nbsp;

• Technical Skills: Knowledge of media systems such as Media Explorer, Prisma, AURA or equivalent.&nbsp;

Skills and Experience

• Effective Communication: Can lead dialogues between and with technical and non-technical people, by presenting a strong case and negotiating well; explains things clearly, challenges ideas effectively and argues in favor of operational processes; determines and utilises the appropriate communication channels; and employs active listening.

• Relationship Management and Account development: Cultivates, nurtures, and grows relationships with key clients and stakeholders, and decision-makers internally, externally, and virtually.

